OVERVIEW: Generate clinical reports from DICOM Structured Report objects

Parse DICOM SR documents and generate professional clinical reports in various
formats.
Supports Basic Text SR, Enhanced SR, Comprehensive SR, and specialized report
types.

Examples:
  dicom-report sr.dcm --output report.txt --format text
  dicom-report sr.dcm --output report.html --format html
  dicom-report sr.dcm --output data.json --format json
  dicom-report sr.dcm --output report.html --format html --style radiology

--style picks a presentation preset (default, cardiology, radiology,
oncology); an unknown value is refused. The SR template (a PS3.16
TID) is read from the document's Content Template Sequence and
shown in the header. --template is a deprecated alias of --style.

Note: PDF format and image embedding are planned for future releases.

USAGE: dicom-report [<options>] <file-path> --output <output>

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to the DICOM SR file

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: text, html, pdf, json, markdown
                          (default: plain text (default))
  --embed-images          Embed images from referenced instances (HTML/PDF only)
  --image-dir <image-dir> Directory containing referenced image files
  --style <style>         Styling preset: default, cardiology, radiology,
                          oncology (section order and colours; not a PS3.16 SR
                          template)
  --template <style>      Deprecated: alias of --style (a styling preset, not a
                          PS3.16 TID)
  --title <title>         Custom report title (overrides SR title)
  --logo <logo>           Path to hospital logo image for branding (PDF/HTML)
  --footer <footer>       Custom footer text for report
  --include-measurements/--no-include-measurements
                          Include measurement tables in output (default:
                          --include-measurements)
  --include-summary/--no-include-summary
                          Include the summary sections (Impressions,
                          Recommendations) in text, HTML and Markdown; the
                          content tree is always rendered (default:
                          --include-summary)
  --language <language>   Report language: en, es, fr, de (default: en)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

